      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T01:23:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In an earlier PS on ag/13237755, Junyu and I discussed using the NetworkCapabilities.NET_CAPABILITY_OEM_* values rather than locally defined constants. Junyu and I agreed to use a bitfield to represent the \"OEM managed\" state after Junyu expressed concern that it\u0027s possible more OEM NetworkCapabilities _could_ be added in the future, and it\u0027s possible that a given network could have more than one of the capabilities.\n\nSince a given network could have multiple OEM capabilities, using the NetworkCapbilities.NET_CAPABILITY_OEM_* values as our constants wouldn\u0027t allow us to bitwise-or the values together in a bitfield. I could create a static map of NetworkCapabilities values mapped to local bitfield values, but I think that would add unnecessary complexity.",
